From b6e72d760d60e547be88f733c8e39e68e21a1a76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:09:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Add Following Pokemon

The first non-egg, non-fainted party member walks behind the player as
an object event (OBJ_EVENT_ID_FOLLOWER). New module src/follower_pokemon.c:

- Spawns/removes/re-skins the follower every overworld frame so it
  matches the current lead (party reorder, fainting, new Pokemon).
- Each player step queues the tile the player left; the follower walks
  there at the player's speed (walk/run/stairs/ice/currents) or hops a
  ledge, which keeps its facing direction in sync.
- Warps, Fly, surfing, biking and cutscene teleports hide the follower on
  the player's tile; it reappears on the next step. Map connection shifts
  are applied to its queue.
- It never blocks the player, trainers' sight or boulders; talking to it
  plays its cry and a friendship-based message.
- 38 species use vanilla overworld sprites; others follow as a Poke Ball
  until more sprites are added to sFollowerGraphics.
- FLAG_SYS_HIDE_FOLLOWER (was unused FLAG_0x8E1) lets scripts hide it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EDbdFFZUtxJmCbg3V6KwVM
